/-! ## §3 — P6 / K4c on a REAL Mina accumulator: the recursion prefix IS the b-polynomial.

`prevChalFoldOk` recomputes the leading `|chalss|` entries of both C8 columns from the carried
challenges and compares. On the real block it holds — so the two numbers the real Wrap proof
exposes for its inherited `sg` accumulators are exactly K4c's `bEval` of the challenges it carries.
This is `sVec_eq_bPoly`'s object, met on a real Mina block for the first time. -/

/-- **`real_recursion_prefix_is_bpoly`** — the real block's C8 recursion prefix is recomputed. -/
theorem real_recursion_prefix_is_bpoly :
    prevChalFoldOk ZETA ZETAW CHALSS EVZ EVZW = true := by decide

/-- **`real_bpoly_values`** — spelled out per accumulator, at both evaluation points. -/
theorem real_bpoly_values :
    bEvalSq ZETA CHALS0 = BP0Z
    ∧ bEvalSq ZETAW CHALS0 = BP0W
    ∧ bEvalSq ZETA CHALS1 = BP1Z
    ∧ bEvalSq ZETAW CHALS1 = BP1W := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide

/-- **`real_bpoly_is_K4c_bEval`** — and the value checked IS K4c's `bEval` (not a lookalike),
by `bEvalSq_eq_bEval`, so `PastaIPA.sVec_eq_bPoly` applies to it. -/
theorem real_bpoly_is_K4c_bEval :
    bEval ZETA CHALS0 = BP0Z ∧ bEval ZETAW CHALS1 = BP1W := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← bEvalSq_eq_bEval]; decide
  · rw [← bEvalSq_eq_bEval]; decide

/-- **`real_recursion_prefix_discriminates`** — a prover that substitutes its own leading entry
(the whole point of getting a recursion accepted) is REFUSED. -/
theorem real_recursion_prefix_discriminates :
    prevChalFoldOk ZETA ZETAW CHALSS (EVZ.set 0 0) EVZW = false
    ∧ prevChalFoldOk ZETA ZETAW CHALSS EVZ (EVZW.set 1 0) = false
    ∧ prevChalFoldOk ZETA ZETAW [CHALS0, CHALS0] EVZ EVZW = false := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide

/-! ## §4 — C8 on the REAL Wrap object, recursion prefix included.

K5's `combinedInnerProduct` over all 47 entries reproduces the `combined_inner_product`
`proof.oracles(...)` computed for the real block. At `KimchiRealProofGate` the same formula had 45
entries and no recursion prefix; here the first two entries are the fold of §3. -/

/-- **`real_cip`** — the shipped C8 formula reproduces the real block's aggregated opening value. -/
theorem real_cip : cipR VV UU EVZ EVZW = CIP := by decide

/-- **`real_cip_discriminates`** — every single tamper of the C8 inputs breaks it. -/
theorem real_cip_discriminates :
    cipR VV UU EVZ EVZW = CIP
    ∧ ¬ (cipR (VV + 1) UU EVZ EVZW = CIP)
    ∧ ¬ (cipR VV (UU + 1) EVZ EVZW = CIP)
    ∧ ¬ (cipR VV UU (EVZ.set 0 0) EVZW = CIP)
    ∧ ¬ (cipR VV UU EVZ (EVZW.set 46 0) = CIP) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide

/-- **`real_cip_is_shipped`** — and `cipR` IS the shipped `combinedInnerProduct` for every field
(`cipR_eq`), so the number above is the shipped def's arithmetic. -/
theorem real_cip_is_shipped {K : Type} [Field K] (a b : K) (x y : List K) :
    cipR a b x y = combinedInnerProduct a b x y := cipR_eq a b x y

/-! ## §5 — the witnessed inverse of the C5 denominator, at the real Wrap values. -/

/-- **`real_denominator_inverse`** — `DINV` is the genuine inverse of `(ζ − ω^{n−3})(ζ − 1)`,
checked in the ring, so no `Field (ZMod qN)` instance is needed. -/
theorem real_denominator_inverse : DENOM * DINV = 1 := by decide

/-! ## §6 — C5 (`ft_eval0`) on the REAL Wrap object.

The shipped `ftEval0R` at the real Wrap domain `n = 16384 = 2^14`, the real
`ω = domain.group_gen`, and the real challenges. Every input was checked in Rust to reproduce
`proof.oracles(...).ft_eval0` before it was written here.

⚑ COST NOTE, measured: `ftEval0R` raises `ω` to `n−3`, `n−2`, `n−1` and `ζ` to `n` through
`Monoid.npow`, which is unary. At `KimchiRealProofGate`'s `n = 32` that is nothing; at the real
Wrap `n = 2^14` it is ~65k kernel multiplications in `ZMod qN`. `bEvalSq`/`sqIter` exist because
K5 already hit this wall on the b-polynomial; C5 has no such ladder. -/

set_option maxRecDepth 100000 in
/-- **`real_zk_polynomial`** — `zkPolyR` at the real domain IS the permutation vanishing
polynomial kimchi evaluated (`PVP`, dumped from `index.permutation_vanishing_polynomial_m()`). -/
theorem real_zk_polynomial :
    (ZETA - OMEGA ^ (N - 3)) * (ZETA - OMEGA ^ (N - 2)) * (ZETA - OMEGA ^ (N - 1)) = PVP := by
  decide

set_option maxRecDepth 100000 in
/-- **`real_ft_eval0`** — the shipped C5 formula reproduces the real block's `ft_eval0`. -/
theorem real_ft_eval0 :
    ftEval0R N OMEGA ZETA BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV = FT0 := by
  decide

set_option maxRecDepth 100000 in
/-- **`real_ft_eval0_discriminates`** — and it is load-bearing on the real values. -/
theorem real_ft_eval0_discriminates :
    ¬ (ftEval0R N OMEGA ZETA (BETA + 1) GAMMA A0 A1 A2 WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV = FT0)
    ∧ ¬ (ftEval0R N OMEGA ZETA BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW (PZ + 1) LCT DINV = FT0)
    ∧ ¬ (ftEval0R N OMEGA ZETA BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ (LCT + 1) DINV = FT0) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide

/-! ## §7 — the COMPOSED P6 decision, on the real Mina block.

`kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec` is the whole assembled decision: C1 at the real index
(`shapeOkRec`), the `prev_challenges` count, the C8 recursion fold (§3), C8 itself (§4), the
witnessed inverse (§5) and C5 (§6). Everything it consumes here came off a real devnet block that
o1-labs' own Kimchi verifier accepted. -/

set_option maxRecDepth 100000 in
/-- **`real_block_accepts`** — the assembled decision ACCEPTS a real Mina block. -/
theorem real_block_accepts :
    kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec IDX_PREV PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 N
      VV UU EVZ EVZW CIP OMEGA ZETA ZETAW BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 CHALSS
      WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV FT0 true true true = true := by
  decide

set_option maxRecDepth 100000 in
/-- **`real_block_decision_discriminates`** — each tamper of a load-bearing input REJECTS:
the recursion count, the recursion prefix, the aggregated opening, and `ft_eval0`. -/
theorem real_block_decision_discriminates :
    kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec IDX_PREV PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 N
      VV UU EVZ EVZW CIP OMEGA ZETA ZETAW BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 [CHALS0]
      WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV FT0 true true true = false
    ∧ kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec IDX_PREV PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 N
      VV UU (EVZ.set 0 0) EVZW CIP OMEGA ZETA ZETAW BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 CHALSS
      WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV FT0 true true true = false
    ∧ kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec IDX_PREV PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 N
      VV UU EVZ EVZW (CIP + 1) OMEGA ZETA ZETAW BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 CHALSS
      WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV FT0 true true true = false
    ∧ kimchiVerifyDecisionFieldRec IDX_PREV PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 N
      VV UU EVZ EVZW CIP OMEGA ZETA ZETAW BETA GAMMA A0 A1 A2 CHALSS
      WZ SZ SHIFT ZZ ZZW PZ LCT DINV (FT0 + 1) true true true = false := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide

/-- **`real_block_freeze_would_refuse`** — and the pre-P6 decision, frozen at `prevLen = 0`,
refuses this real block outright: no arithmetic is ever reached. -/
theorem real_block_freeze_would_refuse :
    kimchiVerifyDecisionRec 0 PREV PUBLIC COLUMNS (PERMUTS - 1) COLUMNS 7 1 true true true
      = false := by decide

